  "title": "Taweez against Warts",
  "data": "To treat warts (small, hard, benign growths on the skin, usually on the hand), take seven barley seeds for each wart. Over each seed, recite verses 1-6 of [Surah al-Waqi'ah](A60) (No. 56) seven times; then recite the following verse seven times over each seed too:\nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْجِبَالِ فَقُلْ يَنْسِفُهَا رَبِّىْ نَسْفًا\nWA YAS'ALOONAKA A'NIL JIBAALI FAQUL YANSIFUHAA RABBEE NASFAA\nAnd they ask you about the mountains. Say: My Lord will carry them away from the roots,\nفَيَذَرُهَا قَاعًا صَفْصَفًا لَا تَرٰى فِيْهَا عِوَجًا وَلَا اَمْتًا\nFAYADHARUHAA QAA'AN SAFSAFAN LAA TARAA FEEHAA I'WAJAN WA LAA AMTAA\nthen leave it a plain, smooth level; you shall not see therein crookedness or unevenness. (20:105-107)\nYou may then blow over the seeds. Take one seed at a time and rub it on one wart. Then put all of the seeds in a piece of cloth, tie a stone to the cloth, and throw it into a well.\nThis act is said to be best done in the waning of the moon.\nIt is also recommended for one who has warts to rub them with a piece of salt and recite the last four verses of [Surah al-Hashr](A63) three times:\nلَوْ اَنْزَلْنَا هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنَ عَلٰى جَبَلٍ لَّرَاَيْتَهٗ خَاشِعًا مُّتَصَدِّعًا مِّنْ خَشْيَةِ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَتِلْكَ الْاَمْثَالُ نَضْرِبُهَا لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ (21)\nLAW ANZALNAA HAADHAL QUR'AANA A'LAA JABALIL LARA'AYTAHOO KHAASHI'AM MUTASADDI'AM MIN KHASHYATILLAAHI WA TILKAL AMTHAALU NADRIBUHAA LIN NAASI LA'ALLAHUM YATAFAKKAROON\nHad We sent down this Qur'an on a mountain, you would certainly have seen it falling down, splitting asunder because of the fear of Allah; and We set forth these parables to men that they may reflect.\nهُوَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ۚ عٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ ۚ هُوَ الرَّحْمٰنُ الرَّحِيْمُ (22)\nHUWALLAAHUL LADHEE LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWA A'ALIMUL GHAYBI WASH SHAHAADATI HUWAR RAHMAANUR RAHEEM\nHe is Allah, besides Whom there is no god; the Knower of the unseen and the seen; He is the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nهُوَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ۚ اَلْمَلِكُ الْقُدُّوْسُ السَّلٰمُ الْمُؤْمِنُ الْمُهَيْمِنُ الْعَزِيْزُ الْجَبَّارُ الْمُتَكَبِّرُ ؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ (23)\nHUWALLAAHUL LADHEE LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWAL MALIKUL QUDDOOSUS SALAAMUL MU'MINUL MUHAYMINUL A'ZEEZUL JABBAARUL MUTAKABBIRU SUBHAANALLAAHI A'MMAA YUSHRIKOON\nHe is Allah, besides Whom there is no god; the King, the Holy, the Giver of peace, the Granter of security, the Guardian over all, the Mighty, the Supreme, the Possessor of every greatness. Glory be to Allah from what they set up (with Him).\nهُوَ اللّٰهُ الْخَالِقُ الْبَارِئُ الْمُصَوِّرُ لَهُ الْاَسْمَاۤءُ الْحُسْنٰى ؕ يُسَبِّحُ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ (24)\nHUWALLAAHUL KHAALIQUL BAARI'UL MUSAWWIRU LAHUL ASMAA'UL HUSNAA YUSABBIHU LAHOO MAA FIS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDI WA HUWAL A'ZEEZUL HAKEEM\nHe is Allah, the Creator, the Maker, the Fashioner; His are the most excellent names; whatever is in the heavens and the earth declares His glory; and He is the Mighty, the Wise.\nThe piece of salt may then be thrown into an oven, and the person with warts may pass over it quickly. The warts will then vanish, Allah willing.\nThe author of the book al-Khaza'in mentions that warts may vanish when they are covered with hair-removing powder."
